# Generic names for shared UI

Icons in `libs/ui/src/icons` and other common components (`@cms/ui`,
`src/shared/`) are named for the **glyph or role**, not the first page or
module that needed them. A later MFE must be able to import the same symbol
without a Tax/Zone/Recommendation prefix. Page-owned files under
`pages/<PageName>/` may stay feature-specific (`TaxAuthorityTablePanel`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — first consumer baked into the name
SettingsTaxAuthorityIcon
SettingsTaxCodeIcon
RecommendationPinIcon
TaxSetupCallout

// ✅ GOOD — reusable anywhere
BuildingIcon
DocumentEditIcon
MapPinIcon
Callout
```

File names follow the export: `building-icon.tsx` → `BuildingIcon`. Do not add
a `Settings*` prefix unless the mark is unique to the Setup category grid.
Do not mass-rename existing Setup-grid icons unless asked.
